WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.362
Hybrid resolution in AWS runs
through two kinds of endpoint.

2
00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:08.389
An inbound endpoint lets outside
resolvers forward queries

3
00:00:08.389 --> 00:00:12.337
into a VPC and get the answers
it sees, private zones included.

4
00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:16.276
It has at least two addresses,
in different Availability Zones.

5
00:00:16.276 --> 00:00:20.632
Each address handles up to
10,000 UDP queries per second,

6
00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:24.137
but as few as 1,500 under
connection tracking.

7
00:00:24.137 --> 00:00:28.356
It speaks plain DNS, DNS over HTTPS,

8
00:00:28.356 --> 00:00:34.987
and a FIPS 140-2 version of
DNS over HTTPS, inbound only.

9
00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:40.325
A second type, the delegation inbound
endpoint, answers NS delegations.

10
00:00:40.325 --> 00:00:44.244
An outbound endpoint goes the
other way: it sends queries that

11
00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:48.163
match a forwarding rule from the
VPC to the agency's resolvers.

12
00:00:48.163 --> 00:00:55.588
It speaks only plain DNS and DNS over
HTTPS, so there's no FIPS option outbound.

13
00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.660
And sharing a rule shares
its outbound endpoint too.
